    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1141-a1">

                <pb facs="1222" n="1126" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1126"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ministry of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-10-17"><hi rendition="#italic">October 17,
                        1898</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William R. Finch</hi>,<lb/><hi
                        rendition="#italic">Envoy Extraordinary and Minister Plenipotentiary of the
                        United States</hi>.</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Minister</hi>: I have the honor to inform your
                    excellency, in response to your notes dated the 7th and 13th instant, that the
                    minister of war and marine has given the necessary orders for the dismissal of
                    the man John B. Dick from the Fifth Regiment of Cavalry, Uruguayan army,
                    together with full pay and proper discharge papers.</p>
                <p>I avail myself of this opportunity,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jacobo A. Varela</hi>,</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
